@flexiarg math-formalization-MG/chart-a-polytope-sphere-by-perimeter-walk
@title Chart a Polytope Sphere by a Perimeter Walk
@keywords Lean, polytope, norm-sphere, chart, perimeter, affine, puncture
@audience lean-provers
@tone heuristic
@provenance retro-promotion pass (2026-08-16), source memory e-84690e27-6853-402d-bdbb-aa48c5f56825

! conclusion:
  For a polyhedral norm sphere, use an explicit piecewise-affine perimeter walk
  when inner-product sphere charts are unavailable.

  + context: The unit sphere is the boundary of a finite polytope, but standard
    stereographic APIs require an InnerProductSpace instance the norm lacks.

  + HOWEVER: Prove edge coverage, seam agreement, and injectivity on the chosen
    half-open parameter interval; a geometric picture does not discharge these.

  + THEN: Enumerate oriented faces or edges, parameterize each affinely, weld the
    endpoints, and rotate the parameter cut when a miss-a-point argument requires
    the excluded point to lie at the seam.

  + BECAUSE: The explicit walk matches the actual norm geometry and reduces the
    chart to affine calculations without importing false Euclidean structure.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Enumerate the boundary pieces in cyclic order.]
    next[Define and verify the piecewise-affine walk.]
    next[Move the cut to the excluded point when needed.]
